The pass's single hash-moving commit. XxHash64 (the reference XXH64
algorithm, written in-repo like PCG32 — the dependency law forbids
twox-hash) implements the same incremental surface as Fnv1a64:
new/seeded, write_bytes/u8/u16/u32/u64/i32/i64 (little-endian), finish.
Golden-tested against reference vectors over the 0..len byte sequences
at stripe boundaries 31/32/33 with a nonzero seed, plus a
chunking-invariance property (any write split digests to the one-shot
value).

The canonical call sites (sim state hash, fixture + content bundle
hashes) now route through XxHash64; the byte encodings are unchanged,
so STATE_ENCODING_VERSION and the replay format_version stay put
(A-087; no replay files exist in the wild). Fnv1a64 remains for the
replay file checksum — a file-format concern, not the canonical state
hasher.

Every pinned golden re-pinned with its written reason: determinism.rs
(ticks 0/30/60 + final), ai.rs (tick 0 + flagship final),
match_rules.rs (the pinned-trail guard), tools' ai_match golden. New
pins: demo 0xb6fff6659cfb7709 (seed 7, 300 ticks), flagship
0x6e9a18bd7c5f699f (seed 7, 7200 ticks), content hash
0x9bc18c521107b262 / map id 0xd38136401ab02ff1. Doc citations updated
(ALPHA_DECLARATION A1/A2 rows, AI-Handoff §2/§4/§5/§6/§7, ARCHITECTURE,
README); DEBT-001 → repaid (M10.1); A-087 logged.

Verified: fmt/clippy clean; 402 dev / 397 release tests green; replay
round-trip PASS on a freshly recorded file (11 checkpoints); content-
validate PASS at the new identity; two-run determinism identical (the
escape hatch did not fire).
