Subject: [PATCH 2/5] =?UTF-8?q?feat(client):=20--seed,=20--record,=20and?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20the=20F8=20bug-report=20dump=20(plan=20=C2=A711.6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The README promises "a report that includes the seed and the tick is a
reproducible incident" — the windowed client could not produce that
report. Now it can, and A14 gets its evidence channel:

- `--seed <u64>` (default 7, mirroring --frames's parser conventions)
  threads into the MatchSetup; restart keeps reproducing the same match
  (the controller seeds derive from it, A15's property).
- `--record <path>` writes the run's replay at match end / clean exit /
  window close (the exiting hook), assembled exactly like the tools'
  AI-match recorder — content hash, map id, the host's command log
  (rejections included), the checkpoint trail collected from the
  per-frame outcomes, the forced final hash. `tools replay-verify`
  accepts the file (A2 at the client seam).
- **F8 — the §11.6 deterministic bug-report dump**: a
  `pandemonium-report-<seed>-tick<tick>.pdrp` replay record plus a
  sidecar `…-info.txt` (seed, tick, content hash, map id, player
  slot, frame count, selection size, the controls line in effect —
  no wall-clock, no paths), written beside --record's path or the
  working directory, both filenames printed, with the existing ping
  cue so the tester sees it wrote. Works while paused (the dump reads
  current state).

The assembly lives in the new client module `report.rs` as pure
functions over host state (replay_record, sidecar_text, report_stem,
write_files) with the tests: the record decodes and re-simulates to
identical hashes (the A2 pattern), F8 during pause produces a valid
record, the sidecar is deterministic per state, the stem is a pure
function. Parser tests cover --seed (valid / missing / garbage),
--record, and --frames's new slice signature. Zero golden movement —
client-only (the repo pins re-verified bit-identical).

Windowed verification under Xvfb + llvmpipe with XTEST injection
(DEBT-008's recipe): --seed 42 runs and diverges from seed 7; --record
writes at the --frames exit and replay-verifies PASS; two F8 presses
land (one mid-run, one during pause) and both dumps replay-verify
PASS; the .pdrp is byte-identical across same-tick presses.
